From 052fc7361b1f6f21dd2e4ead38343855f576bd56 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ananthchellappa <ananth.chellappa@outlook.com>
Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 18:02:11 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] frontend: report an .op card with no netlist instead of
 aborting

A deck of a title line and an .op card -- six bytes, no netlist at all --
reaches assert(plot_cur->pl_dvecs != NULL) in ft_cktcoms() and dies on
SIGABRT.  Measured on ngspice-46 as released:

    $ printf '*\n.op\n' > tiny.cir
    $ ngspice --batch -n tiny.cir ; echo rc=$?
    ngspice: ../../../src/frontend/dotcards.c:225: ft_cktcoms: Assertion `plot_cur->pl_dvecs != NULL' failed.
    rc=134

The analysis is not what fails.  The operating point runs to completion and
prints "No. of Data Rows : 1"; only the dot-card epilogue dies.  Because
abort() does not flush stdio, that output is discarded whenever stdout is a
file or a pipe, so a caller running in batch mode gets 0 bytes on stdout,
106 bytes of assertion text on stderr, and rc=134.

.op is the only analysis this can reach.  DCop() passes a NULL refName to
OUTpBeginPlot() (src/spicelib/analysis/dcop.c:50) because an operating point
has no sweep to plot against, so run->refIndex stays -1 and no data
descriptor is added for a reference vector.  Every other analysis passes one
-- DCtran() passes "time", .ac a frequency, .dc a sweep -- so its plot holds
at least that column and is never empty.  beginPlot() has the exact test for
this state in the second disjunct of its "nothing to save" guard
(src/frontend/outitf.c:461): numData == 0 with refIndex == -1.  But the guard
is gated behind numNames &&, and CKTnames() returns numNames == 0 for a
circuit with no non-ground node (CKTmaxEqNum - 1).  So the guard declines,
plotInit() runs, and pl_dvecs stays NULL.

The assertion is therefore standing on a property of the user's deck, not on
an invariant of the program.  Replace it with a test, a diagnostic and a
return, in the idiom the same function already uses for !ft_curckt twenty
lines above; main.c turns the return into the process's exit status.  The
result is rc=1 with the netlist named on stderr, which is what .tran, .dc
and .ac on the identical netlist have always done.

Putting the guard in beginPlot() instead -- dropping the numNames &&
conjunct so the existing E_NOTFOUND path fires -- was measured and rejected:
it fails tests/regression/misc/empty-1.cir, which runs op, tran and ac on a
zero-node circuit from a .control block and is titled "check that we can
survive emptiness".  All three analyses stop at "Error: no data saved for
...; analysis not run" and the committed .out loses its Initial Transient
Solution block.  It also turns three unrelated nodeless decks (.print tran,
.print ac, .four) from rc=0 into rc=1, and stops the -r route writing a
rawfile for a nodeless .tran, which today writes a valid one-column file.

The last clause of the message is "no operating point printed!" rather than
main.c's "no simulations run!" because the operating point did run and says
so on the line above.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/frontend/dotcards.c | 14 +++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/frontend/dotcards.c b/src/frontend/dotcards.c
index 60a3e1a..2acadf1 100644
--- a/src/frontend/dotcards.c
+++ b/src/frontend/dotcards.c
@@ -222,7 +222,19 @@ ft_cktcoms(bool terse)
     /* If there was a .op line, then we have to do the .op output. */
     plot_cur = setcplot("op");
     if (plot_cur != NULL) {
-        assert(plot_cur->pl_dvecs != NULL);
+        /* An operating point has no reference vector, so its plot holds one
+           vector per output column and nothing else.  A circuit with no
+           non-ground node yields no columns, and the plot is empty.  That is
+           a property of the deck, not an invariant of this program, so it is
+           reported and returned the way the ft_curckt guard above does --
+           main.c turns the return into the process's exit status. */
+        if (plot_cur->pl_dvecs == NULL) {
+            fprintf(cp_err,
+                    "Error: incomplete or empty netlist\n"
+                    "       or no node to report an operating point for;\n"
+                    "no operating point printed!\n");
+            return 1;
+        }
         if (plot_cur->pl_dvecs->v_realdata != NULL) {
             if (terse) {
                 fprintf(cp_out, "OP information in rawfile.\n");
-- 
